## Context

Child of 0700. Backward and forward citation search from the ICF works retained
by 1655. Decision of the 29 September consultation: two rounds; a third only if
the second brings admissible works. Rerun conditions: interrupted query, missed
sentinel, external reference without decision, incomplete summary.

Baseline integration closes under 1655. Keep uncertain works and sentinel routes
in the seed roster; the fully graded REL set alone is not the discovery universe.
Execution plan and baseline evidence: `docs/rel-corpus-completion-2026-10-08.md`.

Amended 2026-10-10 (author decision, see the log): this ticket is a tracker. The
staged screening it used to own is retired; new works are scored by the pipeline
redesign (`docs/rel-pipeline-redesign-2026-10-10.md`). Children:
- 2061 finish and archive the round-one merge, land the collector as a lane
- 2062 wind down the staged screening half (ledger frozen 2026-10-10)
- 2060 scoring calibration trial on the sealed sets (child of 0700)
- 2063 round two from the scored frontier, third-round decision and closure

Staged plan (author decision 2026-10-10, tracker 2070): 1654 is finished first
through 2061 and 2062 (stage S1). Round two (2063) follows the end-to-end run with
one cheap scorer (2071), because its frontier is chosen by score; this tracker
therefore closes after 2063.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Two rounds run, counts per round (references and citations, duplicates, new works): round one under 2061, round two under 2063
- [ ] Third round triggered or dropped, with the measurement that decides it (2063)
- [ ] New works delivered under the intake contract with provenance and merged (2061, 2063), then scored by the redesign (2060, 2071); venue data and counts reconciled before each round's yield is measured
- [ ] Children 2060 to 2063 closed; this tracker closes only after the integration review
